From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:02:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rga: Don't write past the end of the
 descriptor table

fill_descriptors() checks n_desc > max_desc before it writes the entry at
index n_desc, so it writes one entry past the end of the table before it
gives up, or without giving up when the scatterlist ends right there.

The off-by-one also hid that the table is too small for formats with
more than one memory plane: rga_buf_init() sizes it from the page count
of the sum of the plane sizes, but rga_buf_prepare() starts every plane
at a new entry, so each plane needs its own page count rounded up. With
the check fixed, such buffers would be rejected.

Round up the page count of each plane and stop before index max_desc.

Fixes: a61ff67ffb9d ("media: rockchip: rga: rework buffer handling for multi-planar formats")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-buf.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-buf.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-buf.c
index 47a8d5a4500a..c1814318785e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-buf.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-buf.c
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ static ssize_t fill_descriptors(struct rga_dma_desc *desc, size_t max_desc,
 	dma_addr_t addr;
 
 	for_each_sgtable_dma_page(sgt, &iter, 0) {
-		if (n_desc > max_desc)
+		if (n_desc >= max_desc)
 			return -EINVAL;
 		addr = sg_page_iter_dma_address(&iter);
 		tmp->addr = lower_32_bits(addr);
@@ -79,7 +79,6 @@ static int rga_buf_init(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 	struct rockchip_rga *rga = ctx->rga;
 	struct rga_frame *f = rga_get_frame(ctx, vb->vb2_queue->type);
 	size_t n_desc = 0;
-	u32 size = 0;
 	u8 i;
 
 	if (IS_ERR(f))
@@ -88,9 +87,12 @@ static int rga_buf_init(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 	if (!rga_has_internal_iommu(rga))
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Every plane is a separate buffer whose descriptors start at a new
+	 * entry, so round up the page count of each plane on its own.
+	 */
 	for (i = 0; i < f->pix.num_planes; i++)
-		size += f->pix.plane_fmt[i].sizeimage;
-	n_desc = DIV_ROUND_UP(size, PAGE_SIZE);
+		n_desc += DIV_ROUND_UP(f->pix.plane_fmt[i].sizeimage, PAGE_SIZE);
 
 	rbuf->n_desc = n_desc;
 	rbuf->dma_desc = dma_alloc_coherent(rga->cores[0]->dev,
